{{!--
    "Inhaltsverzeichnis".

    Built client-side from the h2/h3 headings Ghost renders inside .gh-content —
    the theme has no access to the post's heading structure at render time, and
    Ghost's editor does not produce an outline field.

    Stays hidden unless at least two headings are found, so short reports do not
    get a one-item table of contents.
--}}
<nav class="cm-panel cm-toc" data-cm-toc hidden aria-labelledby="cm-toc-title">
    <h2 class="cm-panel-title" id="cm-toc-title">Inhaltsverzeichnis</h2>
    <ol class="cm-toc-list" data-cm-toc-list></ol>
</nav>
